  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company is riding strong retail and e-commerce momentum, with its smart ceiling fans and heaters now stocked at Home Depot, Target, Walmart, Lowe’s, and across a broad online footprint. A strategic partnership to deploy its AI-enabled smart platform as a brand standard in a European hotel group’s portfolio adds international reach. Collaboration with NVIDIA’s AI ecosystem signals future smart-home optionality. The business has logged nine consecutive quarters of year-over-year revenue growth, reflecting solid end-market demand. The narrative leans bullish, but the small-cap profile and consumer-discretionary exposure make the adoption ramp a closely watched execution story.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is pushing an aggressive retail rollout and forging high-profile alliances—including the European hotel group OTT and NVIDIA—to embed its technology. They have delivered improving gross margins and steady revenue progression, and they guide toward cash flow positivity in 2026, supported by sufficient liquidity and recent institutional funding. The upcoming corporate update call serves as a near-term test of retail sell-through traction and project deployment. While the strategy was ambitious, credibility now hinges on visible operational follow-through and sustained channel velocity.",
